.TH LZ4 1
.SH NAME
lz4 \- compress a stream into the LZ4 frame format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lz4
[ infile [ outfile ] ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I lz4
reads its input and writes it as a single LZ4 frame, the format the
standard lz4 tool produces, on the output.  With no arguments, or with
.B -
as a name, the standard input and output are used.
.PP
The input is compressed block by block with bounded memory, so it may
be arbitrarily large.  The one narrowing from standard LZ4 is the match
window: an offset never exceeds 16383 bytes, so the decoder's history
ring fits a 64K address space.  A stream written here is read by
.IR unlz4 (1),
by the standard lz4 tool, and by mxunlz4 on the host.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
unlz4(1), tar(1)
